export anchor EmbeddedPanelStyle:
    number: 218
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Embedded panel
    idea: Brightwork as a guest, a compact 480px panel living inside someone else's page with its own small header, tabs and one quiet plum accent, so it reads clearly as a separate app without fighting the host.
    base: light
    palette:
        hostBackground: #eceef1, the host page, never inside the panel
        hostSkeleton: #d9dde2, grey placeholder bars for host content
        panel: #ffffff, the panel body
        panelSub: #f7f7f9, the KPI strip and panel footer
        line: #e2e3e8, rows, tabs and section rules inside the panel
        text: #1d1b22, names and values
        muted: #5a5764, sub lines, caps headings and times
        plum: #84276f, the active tab, New project button, links, progress, this week bars and focus
        plumTint: #f6e9f2, a focused or selected row
        onTrack: #18733a, text with a circle and tick
        atRisk: #8c5400, text with a triangle and bang
        behind: #b3261e, text with an octagon and cross, and the overdue banner on #fcebea
    type:
        One stack, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica
        Neue, Arial, sans-serif, small throughout. Panel base 13px at
        1.45, the greeting 15px bold, KPI values 17px bold, row names
        13px semibold, activity 12px, sub lines and times 11px, and
        section heads 11px bold uppercase tracked 0.06em.
    layout:
        A host page frames the panel. The host has a white top bar with a
        grey circle logo, the words Team portal and grey skeleton links,
        and a main column of white skeleton cards. The panel sits in a
        480px right column under a small host caption reading Embedded app
        and 480px wide. The panel is one bordered white box. Its header
        row has the plum mark and Brightwork, then a bell, the avatar with
        the name and an open in new window icon. A tab row follows with
        Home underlined in plum, Projects, Tasks, Team and a More
        disclosure at the right holding Reports and Settings. Then a
        search field with a small New project button, then the greeting
        with the date in grey on one line and a slim red banner saying
        4 tasks are overdue with a View link. A four cell KPI strip runs
        edge to edge on the grey sub surface. Projects is a caps head with
        a count and an All projects link over six two line rows, the name
        over team, tasks and due date, then a 64px mini bar, the percent
        and the status. The chart is a short 14 bar chart with last week
        59 and this week 73 stacked beside it. Activity is a tight list
        with 24px initials and short times like 12 min. A grey footer says
        Powered by Brightwork with an Open full app link. Under 1000px the
        panel moves above the host content, centred at up to 480px. Under
        600px the mini bars hide, the search takes a full row with the
        button below it and the week totals sit under the chart.
    spacing: A 4px base. 12px side padding inside the panel, 5px row padding and 24px between the host column and the panel.
    density: Very compact. Everything fits the 480px column, about 1000px tall, with no inner scrolling.
    corners: 8px on the panel, 6px on buttons, fields and host cards, 5px on the banner, round avatars.
    borders: 1px #d3d4db around the panel, 1px #e2e3e8 between rows and sections, 1px #d9dde2 around host cards.
    shadows: One soft lift on the panel only, 0 1px 2px and 0 6px 18px at 8 percent, to separate it from the host.
    icons:
        14px line icons at stroke 2, used sparingly. Status glyphs are 13px,
        a circle with a tick, a triangle with a bang and an octagon with a
        cross, beside a bold 11px word.
    focus: A 2px plum outline offset 2px. A focused row also takes the plum tint, and a focused field a plum border.
    tone: Clipped, such as Due this week, View, All projects and 12 min, with host labels kept neutral.
